---
// Case study: Baby Boom NSK — E-commerce UX Audit & Redesign.
// All wording is taken unchanged from the original Framer site.
// The long dash in this file's name is part of the page address and must stay.
import CaseStudyLayout from '../../layouts/CaseStudyLayout.astro';
import Figure from '../../components/Figure.astro';
import Gallery from '../../components/Gallery.astro';

import categoryGrid from '../../assets/images/baby-boom/01.png';
import nursery from '../../assets/images/baby-boom/02.png';
---

<CaseStudyLayout slug="baby-boom-nsk-—-e-commerce-ux-audit-redesign">
  <section class="container case-section">
    <h2>Project overview</h2>
    <p>
      Baby Boom NSK is an online store specializing in baby products, primarily serving parents,
      relatives, and friends purchasing gifts.
    </p>
    <p class="spaced">
      The objective of the project was to improve usability, strengthen user trust, and simplify the
      purchasing journey through a research-driven UX audit and redesign.
    </p>
    <p>
      The focus was on identifying friction points in navigation and product discovery, and
      delivering clear, structured design improvements.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="container case-section">
    <h2>My role &amp; collaboration</h2>
    <p>I worked as a UX Designer, leading:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>User research</li>
      <li>Usability testing</li>
      <li>UX audit</li>
      <li>Interface redesign</li>
      <li>Visual system refinement</li>
    </ul>
    <p class="spaced">
      I delivered structured UX recommendations and redesigned key screens.<br />Implementation was
      handled by the client’s internal team.
    </p>
    <p>
      Due to budget constraints, not all redesign elements were fully implemented. However,
      redesigned flows were validated through usability testing.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="container case-section">
    <h2>Process</h2>
    <p>I conducted interviews with key user groups — primarily parents and gift buyers.</p>
    <p>Usability testing revealed:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Navigation felt confusing</li>
      <li>Filters were ineffective</li>
      <li>Product information lacked clarity</li>
      <li>Absence of reviews reduced trust</li>
      <li>Product imagery did not feel authentic</li>
    </ul>
    <p>These findings shaped all design decisions.</p>
    <p>Based on research insights, the main usability gaps were identified:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Friction in product discovery</li>
      <li>Inefficient filtering logic</li>
      <li>Inconsistent visual hierarchy</li>
      <li>Weak trust signals</li>
    </ul>
    <p>The core challenge was not visual appearance, but clarity and guidance.</p>
    <p class="spaced">The redesign focused on three strategic goals:</p>
    <p>
      <strong>Simplify navigation</strong><br />Improved menu structure and reduced unnecessary
      steps.
    </p>
    <p>
      <strong>Enhance product discovery</strong><br />Redesigned filters for better precision and
      relevance.<br />Introduced a category carousel to support browsing behavior.
    </p>
    <p>
      <strong>Strengthen trust &amp; clarity</strong><br />Added customer reviews and expanded
      product descriptions.<br />Created a more consistent visual system (typography, colors, UI
      elements).
    </p>
  </section>

  <Gallery
    images={[
      {
        src: categoryGrid,
        alt: 'Two versions of the store’s category grid side by side: one with product photos on a white background, the other with lifestyle photos of babies wearing the products under the heading “Popular categories” in Russian.',
      },
    ]}
  />

  <section class="container case-section">
    <h2>Results</h2>

    <h3 class="subtitle">Outcomes</h3>
    <p>Following redesign validation and client feedback:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Users completed purchase tasks more easily during testing</li>
      <li>Navigation flow became clearer and more intuitive</li>
      <li>Cart abandonment behavior decreased</li>
      <li>The overall perception of professionalism and trust improved</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      While full implementation was limited by budget, usability testing confirmed stronger task
      completion rates and improved user confidence.
    </p>

    <h3 class="subtitle">Client Feedback</h3>
    <p>
      “We thought our website was working well… until we realized how much we were overlooking. Now
      everything feels smoother — and it shows in the business.”<br />— Yulia, Owner of Baby Boom
      NSK
    </p>

    <h3 class="subtitle">Impact</h3>
    <p>
      The redesign went beyond aesthetics. It improved clarity, strengthened trust, and aligned the
      digital experience with the emotional needs of parents and gift buyers.
    </p>
    <p>
      The updated UX positioned Baby Boom NSK as a more modern, coherent, and customer-focused brand.
    </p>
  </section>

  <Figure
    src={nursery}
    alt="A smiling woman sitting on a nursery floor, holding up a white baby bodysuit from an open delivery box."
    size="bleed"
  />
</CaseStudyLayout>
